#X text 20 10 CLOUD 2 - its 6 numbers are gnat\$0[6] .. [11]: position \, spray \, grain size (ms) \, density (grains per second) \, pitch (semitones) \, level. THE CLOCK: every 2 ms the phase gph\$0[1] grows by density x 0.002 \, and each time it passes 1 a grain fires (so a new density acts at once). Each grain gets a start = (position +- spray) of the sound \, a duration = the size but at most 8000 / density ms (so 8 voices are always enough) and a reading speed 2^(pitch / 12) x file rate / Pd rate. The 8 voices take turns. Every voice reads with [tabread4~] under a Hann window., f 105;
#X obj 20 130 loadbang;
#X obj 20 156 metro 2;
#X obj 20 182 expr gph\$0[1] = gph\$0[1] + gnat\$0[9] * 0.002;
#X obj 20 208 moses 1;
#X text 440 182 <- the clock: density x 2 ms per tick, f 26;
#X obj 80 234 t b b;
#X obj 200 260 expr gph\$0[1] = gph\$0[1] - 1;
#X text 440 260 <- passed 1: keep the rest \, and fire a grain, f 26;
#X obj 80 300 t b b b;
#X obj 440 326 expr gnat\$0[11] * 0.5 / sqrt(max(1 \, gnat\$0[9] * min(gnat\$0[8] \, 8000 / max(gnat\$0[9] \, 0.5)) / 1000)), f 34;
#X obj 440 386 s \$0-cg1;
#X text 440 416 ^ loudness: level / sqrt(how many grains overlap) \, so dense clouds do not get louder, f 40;
